# Capability and dependency map

'Sufficient here' is not 'necessary in every possible theory'. Each dependency below refers to the stated model.

| Phenomenon | Sufficient ingredients in this program | Missing/changed ingredient that matters | Status |
|---|---|---|---|
| Operator fusion | One-hot selection, aligned operand frames, pointwise truth functions | Frame mismatch invalidates structural fusion | Paper B proof |
| XOR interference | Linear superposition plus shear and relative nonidentity rotation | No probabilities follow from cancellation | Standard algebra, checked construction |
| Nonseparable states | Field tensor dimension>=2 and suitable reversible mixing | One-hot deterministic-only preparation would exclude them | Known MQT |
| Logical contextuality | Two nonzero Smith factors and complete K-linear basis family | Rank-one support remains local | General trichotomy/Hardy proof |
| Strong contextuality | Leading residue multiplicity h>=2 in the complete bipartite contract | Restricting settings may remove it; two binary settings never suffice in residueF2 | General proofs |
| Exact dense codebooks | Invertible encoding orbit plus unrestricted complete joint K-basis readout | Encoder/decoder restrictions or discard policy change the count | d*h theorem |
| Universal exact teleportation | Full resource injectivity plus complete invertible analyzer and corrections | Nilpotents can preserve support advantage while killing injectivity | Criterion with explicit carriers |
| Binary-rank hierarchy | Literal tensor and unrestricted local field groups | A-linearity retains finer Smith data | Standard rank plus restriction synthesis |
| Exact error correction | Injective error images in direct sum with retained syndrome | Degenerate codes require different conditions | Supporting theorem |
| Standard BV exact query gain | Not available under QXOR characteristic-two exact readout | Amplitude-polynomial span cannot hold2^n independent secrets with q<n | General lower bound |
| Kickback | Shared A-module eigenstate for z=R^2 | An invertible Fourier basis is still absent | Exact identity and rank obstruction |
| UNIQUE-SAT oracle gain | Known unrestricted F2 modal circuit and special promise | Not arbitrary SAT or a bounded-error physical model | Known positive control, reproduced |
| Symbolic modal support | B_A enrichment, chosen effects, nonzero postulate | Bare LM pairing alone insufficient | Sufficient interface theorem |
| Practical folding speed | Potentially favorable structure, efficient recognition, reuse | Generic cuts match reductions; output and preparation costs dominate elsewhere | Empirical question open |

Zero divisors are not necessary for entanglement, Bell/GHZ phenomena, no-cloning or field teleportation. They matter specifically for tensor annihilation, nonprimitive branches, filtration-sensitive classifications and support/injectivity separations. Cyclic R is not necessary for generic modal contextuality; its defensible role is to motivate a particular equivariance restriction. Tensor choice is necessary to state which resources exist, not sufficient to decide every support table without specifying effects.

See the [resource hierarchy](RESOURCE_HIERARCHY.md) for matched equivalences and [negative-result table](../06_NEGATIVE_RESULTS.md) for explicit exclusions.
